.TH BACKGROUND 2 2000-1月 "metpa" "metpa"
.SH NAME
metpa \- Create the gsea background model for metabolism analysis
.SH SYNOPSIS
\fImetpa(\fBkegg\fR as any, 
\fBreactions\fR as any, 
\fBorg_name\fR as string = \fB<NULL>\fR, 
\fBis_ko_ref\fR as boolean = FALSE, 
\fBmultipleOmics\fR as boolean = FALSE, 
[\fB<Environment>\fR]);\fR
.SH DESCRIPTION
.PP
Create the gsea background model for metabolism analysis
.PP
.SH OPTIONS
.PP
\fBkegg\fB \fR\- the kegg [Pathway](cref:T:SMRUCC.genomics.Assembly.KEGG.DBGET.bGetObject.Pathway) model collection of current organism or 
 the KEGG [Map](cref:T:SMRUCC.genomics.Assembly.KEGG.WebServices.XML.Map) data collection.
 andalso could be a tuple list of the idset.
. 
.PP
.PP
\fBreactions\fB \fR\- A collection of the reference [ReactionTable](cref:T:SMRUCC.genomics.Model.Network.KEGG.ReactionNetwork.ReactionTable) model 
 data for build the metabolism network. 
.PP
.PP
\fBorg_name\fB \fR\- the KEGG organism code (or the organism name) of the target model, default \fBNULL\fR.. 
.PP
.PP
\fBis_ko_ref\fB \fR\- 
 treats the given KEGG pathway model as the KO reference model? Default \fBFALSE\fR means
 the pathway model of a specific organism.
. 
.PP
.PP
\fBmultipleOmics\fB \fR\- 
 creates the background model for the multiple omics data analysis? Default \fBFALSE\fR.
. 
.PP
.PP
\fBenv\fB \fR\- the R# runtime environment.. 
.PP
.SH VALUE
.PP
a [metpa](cref:T:SMRUCC.genomics.Analysis.HTS.GSEA.KnowledgeBase.Metabolism.Metpa.metpa) background model for the metabolism enrichment analysis.
.PP
.SH SEE ALSO
background
